ney only in large chunks =0Afrom institutional investors and rich people ca=
n charge 20% of gains, but a =0Amutual fund that takes money in $1,000 incr=
ements from anyone mostly can=E2=80=99t.=0A=0AHere is an intuitive story yo=
u might tell about the effects of this rule:=0A=0A * If you=E2=80=99re very=
 good at picking the stocks that will go up, you would rather =0Ado it for =
institutional investors in a hedge fund or private equity fund [2]  <>=0A (=
and get a cut of your winnings) than for retail investors in a mutual fund =
=0A(and not get a cut). =0A * Over time, the best investors will work at he=
