expensively.Possibly it is better to get above-market =0Aperformance expens=
ively, depending on how expensive. This is a story in which =0Aretail inves=
tors have gotten much betterpricing on their main investment =0A(owning the=
 stock market), but maybe less access to other, cooler investments.=0A=0AYe=
sterday the US Securities and Exchange Commission proposed a bunch of chang=
es=0A <https://bloom.bg/3W1Zl6I> to its rules to allow what it calls =E2=80=
=9Cresponsible =0Aretailization of private markets.=E2=80=9D The basic issu=
e, which we discuss a lot =0Aaround here, is that retail investors can inve=
st in public markets, but not in =0Aprivate companies. Private markets have=
 gotten bigger in recent decades, and =0Anow a lot of the good cool compani=
