ting similar incentives to, for =0Aexample, advisers to regulated funds, su=
ch advisers may be more likely to offer =0Aprivate market strategies to reg=
ulated funds.=0A=0AIf the good investment managers can charge retail client=
s the good fees, the =0Athinking goes, maybe they will sell them the good p=
roducts.=0A=0AThis is not the only possible analysis, of course. The Wall S=
treet Journal =0Anotes <https://bloom.bg/4rDUGDP>:=0A=0AExpanding the pool =
of potential investors is a priority of the private-equity =0Aindustry at a=
 time when many institutions such as pension funds and endowments =0Aare pu=
lling back from the asset class. The industry=E2=80=99s main problem has be=
en its =0Ainability to unload companies at attractive prices, leaving a hug=
e backlog of =0Aunsold assets.=0A=0APrivate-equity fundraising has declined=
