ments section would be designed to test knowledge, =0Acomprehension, and sk=
ills to understand different types of financial =0Astatements, financial st=
atement numeracy, and investment-related ratios and =0Ametrics. For example=
, this section would test candidates=E2=80=99 knowledge of the =0Adifferent=
 types of financial statements (e.g., balance sheets and income =0Astatemen=
ts), GAAP versus non-GAAP financial measures, and valuation ratios and =0Am=
etrics (e.g., debt-to-equity ratio, current ratio, internal rate of return,=
 =0Aand bond calculations such as yield to maturity).=0A=0AThe Conflicts of=
 Interest section would be designed to test knowledge, =0Acomprehension, an=
d skills with respect to a variety of conflicts investors may =0Aencounter =
in exempt offerings. For example, this section would test candidates=E2=80=
=99 =0Aunderstanding of issuer and affiliate conflicts of interest, interme=
diary =0Aconflicts of interest, insider conflicts of interest, and investor=
 conflicts of =0Ainterest (such as tiered information access and other pref=
erential treatment =0Afor certain investors).=0A=0ASounds sophisticated.=0A=
